## 1. Grabbing the source

Repo is a tool provided by Google that simplifies using Git in the context of the Android source:
- Repo docs: http://source.android.com/source/developing.html
- Git docs: http://git-scm.com/book

### 1.1 Installing dependencies and Repo

Several packages are needed in order to build crDroid. Example (we are using Ubuntu):
```bash
sudo apt install bc bison build-essential ccache curl flex g++-multilib gcc-multilib git git-lfs gnupg gperf imagemagick lib32ncurses-dev lib32readline-dev lib32z1-dev liblz4-tool libncurses6 libncurses-dev libsdl1.2-dev libssl-dev libwxgtk3.2-dev libxml2 libxml2-utils lzop pngcrush rsync schedtool squashfs-tools xsltproc zip zlib1g-dev
```
(Some of those packages may need adjustment for your linux distribution)

Install the Repo tool:
```bash
# create ~/bin and add to PATH for this session (or add to your shell profile)
mkdir -p ~/bin
export PATH=~/bin:$PATH

# download Repo
curl https://storage.googleapis.com/git-repo-downloads/repo > ~/bin/repo

# make Repo executable
chmod a+x ~/bin/repo
```

Tip: Add `export PATH=~/bin:$PATH` to `~/.bashrc` or your shell profile so Repo is available in future sessions.

### 1.2 Initializing Repo

Create a workspace and initialize the crDroid 16.0 manifest:
```bash
mkdir -p ~/crDroid
cd ~/crDroid
repo init -u https://github.com/crdroidandroid/android.git -b 16.0 --git-lfs --no-clone-bundle
```

Add the needed manifest for a GSI
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Lost-Entrepreneur439/treble_manifest.git .repo/local_manifests -b lineage-23.2
```

Sync the source tree (may take a long time on first run):
```bash
repo sync
```

Notes and useful flags:
- To recover from interrupted syncs or to force a fresh copy:  
  `repo sync --force-sync --no-tags --no-clone-bundle -j8` (adjust `-j` to match your bandwidth/CPUs).
- Use `repo sync -c` to only sync the current branch per project (saves time/space) when appropriate.

---

## 2. Building

Apply the required patches for a GSI:
```bash
bash crDroid-gsi-MisterZtr-based/patches/apply-patches.sh .
```

Prepare the build environment:
```bash
. build/envsetup.sh
```

Select your device:

For ARM64 Vanilla with ext4:
```bash
breakfast arm64_bvN4
```
Or for A64 (ARM32/Binder64) Vanilla with ext4 (requires https://github.com/Lost-Entrepreneur439/LineageOS-a64_gsi/blob/lineage-23.2/patches/personal/device_phh_treble/0011-Convert-arm64-support-to-a64.patch)
```bash
breakfast a64_bvN4
```

Then to start a build:
```bash
m systemimage -j$(nproc --all)
```

Troubleshooting tips:
- Out-of-disk-space: ensure enough free space (Android tree can require 100+ GB).
- If builds fail after repo sync, try `repo sync --force-sync` and a clean build: `mka clean` then rebuild.

---

## 3. Contributions

To submit changes or patches:
- Fork the repository on GitHub, make your changes, and open a Pull Request against the appropriate branch.
- We review PRs and merge them when appropriate.

---

## 4. Personal Patches & Fixes (Xperia 10 III / PDX213 & Generic GSI)

This fork includes dedicated patches in `patches/personal/` addressing critical GSI issues:

### 4.1 Biometrics & Keystore (Face Unlock for Banking & Bitwarden)
* **Class 3 (`STRENGTH_STRONG`) Face Unlock:** Promoted `SenseProvider` and HIDL face sensor strength from `STRENGTH_WEAK` (Class 2) to `STRENGTH_STRONG` (Class 3), enabling biometric prompt support for password managers (Bitwarden) and banking apps.
* **Token Serialization Fix:** Replaced lossy UTF-8 String conversions with Base64 encoding in `PreferenceHelper.kt` to prevent 69-byte binary `HardwareAuthToken` corruption.
* **Crypto Challenge Binding:** Preserves `mOperationId` in `SenseService.kt` and injects it into the authentication token so Keystore2 verifies cryptographic `CryptoObject` operations properly.
* **Keystore2 TrustZone Software Enforcement:** Configures Qualcomm KeyMint to generate hardware-accelerated keys with `Tag::NO_AUTH_REQUIRED` while Keystore2 handles software biometric authorization, resolving `KEY_USER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED` errors on software face unlock.
* **Biometric SID Verification:** Fixed `KeyStoreCryptoOperationUtils.java` so `Cipher.init()` allows authorization when any registered sensor matches, preventing `KeyPermanentlyInvalidatedException` / `Crypto primitive not initialized` crashes.

### 4.2 microG Suite & Play Store
* Bundled with clean FOSS microG (`GmsCore`, `GsfProxy`, `FakeStore`, `FDroid`, `FDroidPrivilegedExtension`).
* **Optional Google Play Store:** Set `export WITH_CUSTOM_PLAYSTORE=true` and place `PlayStore.apk` into `vendor/microg/FakeStore/` to bundle your own modified Play Store package. Defaults to FOSS `FakeStore.apk`.

### 4.3 Networking, Performance & System UI
* **Hotspot Tethering DNS:** Configured Tethering to automatically advertise `1.1.1.1`, `1.0.0.1`, and `8.8.8.8` upstream DNS servers with legacy DNS proxy fallback.
* **5G NR Network Settings:** Added 5G Preferred Network Type and NR repository support in Settings UI.
* **SurfaceFlinger Blur Toggle:** Reads `persist.sys.phh.sf.background_blur` to enable/disable blurs dynamically.
* **AnimationUtils:** Fixed custom activity transition animation initialization crashes.

### 4.4 RGB Notification LED & Battery Charging Light (Sony Xperia 10 III / PDX213 & Generic GSI)
* **PM6150L Sysfs Node Permissions (`phh-on-boot.sh`):** Fixes `sync_state`, `start_blink`, and `brightness` node ownership to `system:system` (mode `0660`) at boot. Uses path-based detection (`/sys/devices/platform/soc/.../pm6150l.../leds/rgb`) without modifying SELinux labels, preserving Qualcomm vibrator HAL (`vendor.qti.vibrator`) directory scanning.
* **Device Light Capabilities (`lineage-sdk`):** Sets `config_deviceLightCapabilities` to `75` (`LIGHTS_RGB_NOTIFICATION_LED | LIGHTS_RGB_BATTERY_LED | LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED | LIGHTS_BATTERY_LED`), enabling `BatteryService` and `LineageBatteryLights` to drive the LED when charging.
* **Universal App Notification LED Pulse (`frameworks/base`):** Updates `NotificationRecord.java` to always generate default `Light` parameters so `LineageNotificationLights` can auto-calculate per-app LED colors and pulse for modern apps that omit legacy `FLAG_SHOW_LIGHTS`.
* **Device Hardware Overlay (`vendor/hardware_overlay`):** Configures `config_intrusiveNotificationLed = true` with 500ms ON / 2000ms OFF timings in Sony `pdx213` overlay.

